WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.098 --> 00:00:19.320
After school Ben couldn't find Winnie.

2
00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:24.904
So he went with Gaby and Mog to the Monsterville Historical Society.

3
00:00:26.405 --> 00:00:30.948
The historical society was located in an old haunted house on the edge of town.

4
00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.462
"Whoa, look at all this stuff," Mog burst out.

5
00:00:35.482 --> 00:00:37.743
"Yikes," Ben added.

6
00:00:41.805 --> 00:00:44.587
The ground floor of the building was packed with objects.

7
00:00:45.527 --> 00:00:51.190
There were old toys and dusty books and racks crammed with robes, capes, and vests.

8
00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:56.553
Huge mummies and wax monster figures stood along the walls of one room.

9
00:00:57.554 --> 00:01:01.736
File cabinets overflowing with papers and old photographs filled another room.

10
00:01:03.532 --> 00:01:06.414
Gaby scratched her head, looking overwhelmed.

11
00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:10.556
"I hope we can find that painting of Pedro in here.

12
00:01:10.936 --> 00:01:14.338
The building closes at six, and this could take longer than I thought."

13
00:01:14.358 --> 00:01:19.000
"Maybe we can find a guide to help us," Ben said.

14
00:01:19.761 --> 00:01:23.583
They looked around until they finally spotted a mummy wearing a guide badge.

15
00:01:26.024 --> 00:01:27.305
Ben floated over to him.

16
00:01:27.325 --> 00:01:29.286
"Excuse me, sir.

17
00:01:29.766 --> 00:01:33.460
We're looking for a specific painting of Monsterville," he said.

18
00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:37.882
"It's an old painting showing Pedro the Pirate burying his treasure.

19
00:01:38.222 --> 00:01:39.182
Do you know where it is?"

20
00:01:39.202 --> 00:01:41.203
"Second floor.

21
00:01:41.583 --> 00:01:43.884
Outlaws section," the guide said.

22
00:01:43.904 --> 00:01:45.604
"You can't miss it."

23
00:01:45.624 --> 00:01:48.485
"Thanks," Gaby said.

24
00:01:49.245 --> 00:01:51.286
The three of them hurried toward the staircase.

25
00:01:51.306 --> 00:01:55.948
"Hey, Waldo and Winnie just walked in!"

26
00:01:56.308 --> 00:01:56.908
Mog said.

27
00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:01.740
"Why are they here?"

28
00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:02.921
Ben wondered aloud.

29
00:02:02.941 --> 00:02:04.301
"Who cares?"

30
00:02:04.661 --> 00:02:05.301
Gaby said.

31
00:02:05.321 --> 00:02:06.202
"Come on.

32
00:02:06.542 --> 00:02:07.602
Let's find that painting!"

33
00:02:07.622 --> 00:02:11.763
"You two can probably find it on your own," Ben said.

34
00:02:11.783 --> 00:02:13.984
"I'll go say hello to Winnie and Waldo.

35
00:02:14.344 --> 00:02:15.624
Maybe they need some help now."

36
00:02:16.725 --> 00:02:18.265
"Okay," Gaby said.

37
00:02:18.285 --> 00:02:20.046
"But don't tell them about the painting.

38
00:02:20.226 --> 00:02:21.246
That's our clue."

39
00:02:21.266 --> 00:02:22.806
"I will.

40
00:02:23.547 --> 00:02:24.547
I mean, I won't.

41
00:02:25.047 --> 00:02:25.847
Don't worry, Gaby.

42
00:02:26.227 --> 00:02:27.908
I won't say a word about the painting."

43
00:02:29.632 --> 00:02:31.374
Gaby and Mog tore upstairs.

44
00:02:32.414 --> 00:02:35.277
Waldo and Winnie were still standing near the front entrance.

45
00:02:36.217 --> 00:02:39.100
Ben floated up to them as they finished talking to a guide.

46
00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.422
"Hi, Ben," Winnie said.

47
00:02:42.442 --> 00:02:45.365
"How'd you know we were coming to the historical society?"

48
00:02:45.385 --> 00:02:48.427
"I came with Gaby and Mog," Ben said.

49
00:02:48.447 --> 00:02:51.290
"Oh. They're here too?"

50
00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:52.390
Waldo asked.

51
00:02:52.751 --> 00:02:56.694
He sounded funny because he was pinching his nose to stop himself from sneezing.

52
00:02:56.714 --> 00:02:58.996
"Did they find a clue that led here?"

53
00:03:00.052 --> 00:03:01.813
"I can't talk about that, remember?"

54
00:03:02.174 --> 00:03:02.914
Ben replied.

55
00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:04.815
"I'm helping both teams.

56
00:03:05.436 --> 00:03:06.476
What are you guys doing here?"

57
00:03:06.496 --> 00:03:10.699
"We created a Magic Mirror spell," Waldo said.

58
00:03:10.719 --> 00:03:13.001
"Huh?" Ben asked.

59
00:03:13.021 --> 00:03:15.943
"It's a mirror for finding stuff.

60
00:03:16.343 --> 00:03:20.025
But the mirror works only one time," Winnie explained.

61
00:03:20.045 --> 00:03:23.868
"We asked it to show us Pirate Pedro's gold."

62
00:03:23.888 --> 00:03:29.372
"But it showed us an image of a golden compass from Pedro's pirate ship," Waldo said.

63
00:03:30.772 --> 00:03:34.073
"The guide said the compass is definitely here—somewhere."

64
00:03:34.093 --> 00:03:38.875
"When we find it," Winnie added, "we're going to cast another spell.

65
00:03:39.376 --> 00:03:41.116
It'll take us to the burial site."

66
00:03:41.136 --> 00:03:43.797
"Want me to help you look for the compass?"

67
00:03:44.178 --> 00:03:44.938
Ben asked.

68
00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:47.059
"Okay," Winnie said.

69
00:03:47.079 --> 00:03:50.080
"The guide said it's in one of the back rooms."

70
00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:54.522
"We're going to need to get permission to take the compass with us," Waldo said.

71
00:03:54.542 --> 00:03:57.303
"Maybe you can talk with somebody about that?

72
00:03:57.663 --> 00:03:58.203
We got Mr.

73
00:03:58.244 --> 00:03:59.224
Freaky to write a note."

74
00:04:00.624 --> 00:04:02.465
Waldo handed Ben a sheet of paper.

75
00:04:02.485 --> 00:04:06.706
"We told him we're working on a project about pirate ships."

76
00:04:06.726 --> 00:04:11.327
"We didn't want to tell him about the treasure until we found it," Winnie said.

77
00:04:11.347 --> 00:04:13.648
"No problem," Ben said.

78
00:04:13.668 --> 00:04:15.928
"I'll go to the visitors' office.

79
00:04:16.309 --> 00:04:17.629
I think it's on the second floor."

80
00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:27.472
Inside the visitors' office, Ben explained the situation to a bored-looking skeleton.

81
00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:31.801
The skeleton barely looked at Mr.

82
00:04:31.861 --> 00:04:34.201
Freaky's note before stamping it, "Approved."

83
00:04:34.221 --> 00:04:38.362
"Thanks," Ben said.

84
00:04:40.863 --> 00:04:46.285
On his way back downstairs, Ben saw Gaby and Mog staring at a painting in a gold frame.

85
00:04:47.765 --> 00:04:50.406
It showed Pedro as a young pirate skeleton.

86
00:04:51.486 --> 00:04:56.768
He was standing on top of a chest inside a deep hole, looking proud as the sun sank

87
00:04:56.848 --> 00:04:57.428
behind him.

88
00:04:58.224 --> 00:05:02.705
Nearby a few other pirates stood with shovels under a small oak tree.

89
00:05:03.966 --> 00:05:08.247
Mog was quickly sketching the painting as Gaby wrote in a small notepad.

90
00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:12.028
"Hey, Ben!"

91
00:05:12.388 --> 00:05:13.628
Gaby waved excitedly.

92
00:05:13.648 --> 00:05:15.229
"We found the painting!"

93
00:05:15.609 --> 00:05:16.229
Mog said.

94
00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:20.370
"We're not allowed to take a picture of it so I'm trying to draw it."

95
00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:23.971
"We see a bunch of clues," Gaby said.

96
00:05:28.768 --> 00:05:30.510
Ben looked carefully at the painting.

97
00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:37.736
"All I see is the treasure chest, some pirates and Pedro, and a tree."

98
00:05:37.756 --> 00:05:41.319
"Those are all clues," Gaby replied.

99
00:05:41.339 --> 00:05:44.882
"The leaves on the tree show that it was early fall.

100
00:05:45.943 --> 00:05:49.246
The position of the sun and the shadows tell us it was late in the day."

101
00:05:50.687 --> 00:05:51.908
Mog's eyes gleamed.

102
00:05:51.928 --> 00:05:58.837
"And the size of that treasure chest tells us something else—that treasure is huge!"
